                                                               ; ASSERT ptr=0

; ============================================================ ; the schedule and the table swap  ONCE  however many
                                                               ; blocks
                                                               ; ASSERT zero 0:175
                                                               ; ASSERT zero 192:1013
                                                               ; THE KEY SCHEDULE AND THE TABLE SWAP  which is
                                                               ; everything an inverse cipher has to do ONCE  however
                                                               ; many blocks it goes on to decrypt;
;
                                                               ; It runs the schedule FORWARD against the forward S
                                                               ; box  keeping the ten temps the regression will need;
                                                               ; then it clears that table and writes the INVERSE one
                                                               ; into the same cells; It leaves the pointer at the
                                                               ; block's own zero  the inverse table resident  the
                                                               ; last round key in the regression window and the ten
                                                               ; temps standing;
;
                                                               ; THIS IS WHY CBC DECRYPTION TOOK A RESTRUCTURING AND
                                                               ; THE OTHER MODES DID NOT; the forward cipher splits
                                                               ; into a table that is laid once and rounds that run
                                                               ; many times  because its table SURVIVES a block; this
                                                               ; one's does not  it is swapped halfway through  so
                                                               ; there is no prefix of the single file that a caller
                                                               ; could run once; Splitting it here is what makes the
                                                               ; swap a once per message cost instead of a once per
                                                               ; block one; At about sixty six thousand instructions
                                                               ; to clear the forward table and seventeen more to
                                                               ; write the inverse  that is the difference between a
                                                               ; mode that is usable and one that is not;
;
                                                               ; THE SPLIT FALLS WHERE IT DOES SO THE INSTRUCTION
                                                               ; STREAM DOES NOT MOVE; the inverse table's walk home
                                                               ; ends at nought and the per block work opens at nought
                                                               ; so the two concatenated are byte for byte the file
                                                               ; they came from and aes/decrypt128 regenerates
                                                               ; identical; That is the same test the forward split
                                                               ; passed and the same reason the seam is where it is;
;
                                                               ; WHAT A SECOND BLOCK MUST PUT BACK; the rounds next
                                                               ; door REGRESS the window and SPEND the ten temps  so a
                                                               ; caller decrypting more than one block has to keep a
                                                               ; copy of both and restore them before each; That is
                                                               ; fifty six bytes against a hundred and fourteen
                                                               ; million instructions  and the rounds' own entry
                                                               ; contracts police everything else;
;
                                                               ; CONTRACTS ARE RELATIVE and the include's offset
                                                               ; resolves them;
;
                                                               ; TAPE MAP  (relative to the block's own zero)
;   @0x057:0x07e  the temp run{40}  ten four byte schedule temps  WANTED AGAIN
;   @0x0a0:0x0af  window{16}  the last round key  WANTED AGAIN
;   @0x0b0:0x0bf  window{16}  phase one's own  spent  and cleared next door
;   @0x0f3:0x3f5  group 0 and the table  forward  then INVERSE

; ============================================================ ; phase one : the key schedule  with the FORWARD table
                                                               ; the first four words ARE the key and they stay in the
                                                               ; window; the earlier cut also copied them into a 176
                                                               ; byte schedule  which is gone

; ============================================================ ; the forward S box is written into the tape
  >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>
  >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>   ; continued
  >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>   ; continued
  >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>   ; continued
  >>>>>>>>>>>>>>                                               ; continued
                                                               ; ASSERT ptr=246
                                                               ; S the AES S box  two hundred and fifty six entries
                                                               ; one to a line laid out for the stride three walk:
                                                               ; datum  walker  trail  so each entry is followed by a
                                                               ; step of three; the caller walks in to the first datum
                                                               ; and back out from the last;
;
                                                               ; FIPS 197 section 5 point 1 point 1; DERIVED and not
                                                               ; typed  and the form is the one sha256/hashcore uses
                                                               ; for its round constants: a comment naming the value
                                                               ; then a delta coded run  shorter direction  which
                                                               ; leans on the cell wrapping at 256 and halves the
                                                               ; cost;
;
                                                               ; It is the multiplicative inverse in GF(2^8) then an
                                                               ; affine transform; block/invsbox256 is the same
                                                               ; permutation read backwards; S of 0x00 is 0x63
