                                                               ; ASSERT ptr=0
                                                               ; THE INVERSE ROUNDS  and nothing else; no schedule and
                                                               ; no table;
;
                                                               ; Entered at the block's own zero with THE CIPHERTEXT
                                                               ; AT @0x0c0:0x0cf  the inverse table resident  the last
                                                               ; round key in the regression window and the ten temps
                                                               ; standing; It leaves the plaintext in the state at
                                                               ; @0x0d3:0x0e2;
;
                                                               ; block/aes128dsetup puts all of that there and its
                                                               ; header says why the two are separate files at all;
;
                                                               ; IT SPENDS WHAT IT IS GIVEN; the window is REGRESSED a
                                                               ; word at a time down to the original key and the ten
                                                               ; temps are consumed on the way  so a caller running a
                                                               ; second block must restore both from a copy taken
                                                               ; after the setup; Fifty six bytes; The alternative was
                                                               ; to regenerate them  which cannot be done  because
                                                               ; regenerating them needs the FORWARD table and that is
                                                               ; the one thing the setup threw away;
;
                                                               ; AND EVERYTHING ELSE IT NEEDS CLEAR  IT CHECKS; the
                                                               ; two zero contracts below the clears are not
                                                               ; decoration: they are what tells a mode that its
                                                               ; restore set was too small  at the block that first
                                                               ; reuses a dirty cell rather than three rounds later in
                                                               ; a wrong byte; They were already here when this was
                                                               ; one file  where they could only ever be true; here
                                                               ; they do work;
;
                                                               ; CONTRACTS ARE RELATIVE and the include's offset
                                                               ; resolves them;
;
                                                               ; TAPE MAP  (relative to the block's own zero)
;   @0x000        cnt
;   @0x053:0x056  scratch for the downward turn
;   @0x057:0x07e  the temp run{40}  SPENT
;   @0x07f:0x082  scratch for the upward turn
;   @0x083:0x09b  aes/xorword pasted at 131
;   @0x09c:0x09f  g{4}
;   @0x0a0:0x0af  window{16}  REGRESSING in place  down to the original key
;   @0x0b0:0x0bf  cleared below  it is phase one's leavings
;   @0x0c0:0x0cf  the ciphertext  which the caller puts here
;   @0x0d3:0x0e2  state{16}  the plaintext comes back here
;   @0x0e3:0x0f2  the round key
;   @0x0f3:0x3f5  the INVERSE table  read only here

                                                               ; the ciphertext comes up to the state  where it stays
                                                               ; sixteen bytes  nineteen cells
